			"notes": {
				"rationale": "bewog is the Präteritum of bewegen in DWDS's sense 2, to induce someone to act, which conjugates strong: bewog, bewogen, Konjunktiv II bewöge. Moving something 🔃 conjugates weak (bewegte). 🫸 stands in for the push that moves a decision. In this sense bewegen takes zu + Dat (jemanden zu etwas bewegen): the free ADV dazu fills that slot, so the valency evidence records zu with no member (de/pronominal-adverb-stands-alone)."
			},
